@page
@model PantheonModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The Pantheon";
}

<section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
        <p class="section-label">Six Gods, Six Schools</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">The Pantheon</h2>
        <div class="ornament-divider" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="200" height="30"><use href="#divider-ornament" /></svg></div>
        <p>
            Every spell a Hollow-touched soul learns traces back to one of six gods. To study a
            school of magic is to petition a god, whether the caster admits it or not. There is
            said to be a seventh, but no shrine has ever borne his mark, and no priest has ever
            spoken his name.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="section-inner section-inner-spaced">
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ankh-icon" /></svg>
                <p class="card-discipline">Healing</p>
                <h3>Saelia, the Calm</h3>
                <p>Goddess of healing and calm nature, whose favor mends what war and ruin break.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#lightning-icon" /></svg>
                <p class="card-discipline">Chaos</p>
                <h3>Vorreth, the Storm</h3>
                <p>God of wild chaos and disaster, called upon by those who court ruin on purpose.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#skull-icon" /></svg>
                <p class="card-discipline">Necromancy</p>
                <h3>Morvane, the Vile</h3>
                <p>God of evil and necromancy, whose following keeps to the dark corners of every town.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#gauntlet-icon" /></svg>
                <p class="card-discipline">War</p>
                <h3>Kaldrun, the Fist</h3>
                <p>God of war and strategy, honored by soldiers before every campaign.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#mask-icon" /></svg>
                <p class="card-discipline">Illusion</p>
                <h3>Ryneth, the Fool</h3>
                <p>God of trickery and illusion. Old rumor claims he has long gone silent. No one can confirm it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#lyre-icon" /></svg>
                <p class="card-discipline">Arts</p>
                <h3>Senneva, the Song</h3>
                <p>Goddess of arts, love, and beauty. Some say no temple to her still stands.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="section-footnote">
            Ready to see it for yourself? <a asp-page="/Index" asp-fragment="download">Check the Hollowbourn download page</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
